  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "A. Correct order <math><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> (ionization energy) <br/>for isoelectronic species (I.E. <math><mo>∝</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></mrow></msub></math> ) <br/>B. Correct order <math><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> (2nd I.E.) <br/>Second electron removal from oxygen requires more energy as it acquires stable <math><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math> configuration after removal of one electron. <br/>C. <math><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></math> (Electronegativity) <br/>In general EN increases in boron family from top to bottom due to increase in <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></mrow></msub></math> on valence shell while boron has highest E.N. due to its vary small size. <br/>D. Correct order <math><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> (Ionic radius) <br/>Ionic radius depends on <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></mrow></msub></math> and number of shells.",
